    "candidate_1": "The nutritionist target decision alone consumed 0.299s across four calls and nutritionist credential revision construction consumed 0.106s across four calls. This shows removable work exists for coach-only scenarios, but the counterfactual coach_only fixture was not measured and suite-wide savings remain unknown.",
    "candidate_2": "The three private-draft tests use corpus() although their assertions do not require a published parent. Aggregate stage means suggest roughly 1.0s of current approval/publication lifecycle per corpus call before accounting for the lighter owner/profile helper. This is a gross estimate, not measured net savings. A real owner/profile-only fixture appears the more promising next narrow candidate, provided characterization confirms no hidden dependency on approved/published state.",
    "root_cause": "No production defect or full-backend timeout root cause was established. This diagnostic only measured four tests.",
    "recommendation": "Do not alter product code or acceptance limits. If a new authorization is issued, first add a real owner/profile-only fixture and use it only in the three private-draft tests, with explicit characterization and preserved published-parent coverage. Defer broad coach_only substitutions until the targeted fixture change is validated."
